  Hype usually rewards tools that look impressive in a demo. Real utility rewards tools that hold up on a Tuesday afternoon, when you need cleaner code, faster research, or less mental clutter. That’s why niche names like **Goblin Tools**, **Gumloop**, **Napkin.ai**, **Tabnine**, and **Codeium** often gain traction person by person, not banner by banner.
  
  > _In 2026, the most-talked-about AI tool in the right circle isn’t always famous. It’s the one people keep using after the novelty wears off._
  
