  ## Frequently asked questions
  
  What is the best AI tool for marketing in 2026?
  
  The best AI tool for marketing depends entirely on the task. For writing long content Claude scores highest. For deep research and broad applications ChatGPT is strong. For SEO-optimised content Surfer SEO or NeuronWriter are more relevant. Those who want to automate video ads look at Arcads. Those who want to build workflows without code start best with Gumloop or Make.com. The key is task-oriented thinking: what output do you need, and which model is specifically trained for that?
  
  What is the difference between n8n and Gumloop?
  
  Both are no-code automation tools, but with a fundamentally different starting point. N8n is open-source and self-hostable, making it the most GDPR-friendly option for Belgian and European businesses. It now also has AI nodes, but these were added later. Gumloop was built AI-native from the ground up: every node can call an AI model for reasoning, categorising or generating. For simple app connections n8n or Make.com suffice. For complex, AI-driven workflows Gumloop is stronger.
  
  Can I also show physical products with Arcads?
  
  Partially. Arcads is excellent for talking-head UGC-style videos where an AI actor takes the floor. You can upload a product photo so the model has context, but the actor cannot hold or demonstrate a physical product on screen. For physical product demos you combine Arcads for the talking-head with separate product images, or work with real UGC creators for that specific format.
  
  Is Recraft V3 better than Midjourney?
  
  For pure aesthetics Midjourney is still a benchmark for photorealistic and artistic images. Recraft V3 ranks number 1 on the Hugging Face Text-to-Image Leaderboard and has two unique strengths: text in images, where Midjourney regularly fails, and vector generation in SVG format. If you need logos, icons, SVG files or print-ready material in CMYK, Recraft V3 is the only serious AI option.
  
  Which AI tool do I use for SEO and GEO?
  
  For SEO-optimised content Surfer SEO, Frase and NeuronWriter are the strongest options. NeuronWriter delivers full SEO functions for 23 euros per month. Those who also want to know how their brand appears in AI search engines like Perplexity or ChatGPT need a tool for generative engine optimisation (GEO) such as Sight AI. The boundary between classic search engine optimisation and GEO is blurring rapidly.
  
  What is the best free AI tool for meetings?
  
  Fathom is the strongest free option: unlimited recordings and transcriptions, no bot visible in the meeting and automatic summary afterwards. Granola is a good alternative: it also does not enter your meeting as a bot and processes the audio discreetly in the background. Tl;dv offers free unlimited recordings and adds coaching highlights for sales and recruitment teams.
  
  Is NotebookLM free?
  
  Yes, NotebookLM is fully available for free via notebooklm.google.com. You load your own documents, PDFs and web pages into it and ask questions about them. The model answers exclusively based on what you have provided, which rules out hallucinations. There is also a paid NotebookLM Plus version with higher capacity limits and extra team functions.
  
  How do I start with AI automation as a non-developer?
  
  Start with one repetitive task that costs you time every week: compiling a report, qualifying leads or publishing content to multiple channels. Tools like Gumloop and Make.com let you build those workflows via drag-and-drop without code. Want to know which automations deliver the most for your business? ClickForest helps you with concrete implementation via clickforest.com/en/ai-for-growth/marketing-automation.
  
